FXStreet (11 Nov, Joshua Gibson) states most of the claim:
- the euro is 57.6% of DXY;
- the euro is down about 5% since late August and fell below 1.1100 for the first time since May 2025;
- the euro accounts for about 2.7 of DXY's 3.4-point rise from the August low to 6 Nov;
- the Fed broad dollar index is up about 2% this year against about 4% for DXY;
- the dollar is down more than 4% against the yuan, and USD/JPY is just under 160;
- Lagarde leaves on 7 Feb 2027, announced the same day as the 29 Oct decision, with no successor named, ahead of France's April election.
The figure '3.6% below the April-2025 tariff-day level' is not in that article, but FRED confirms it: the broad index was 121.88 on 6 Nov against 126.38 on 2 Apr 2025 (-3.56%). FRED's H.10 data also show:
- the broad index up 1.8% this year to 6 Nov;
- EUR/USD falling from 1.1684 (21 Aug) to 1.1034 (13 Nov), -5.6% and its lowest daily rate since Apr 2025;
- USD/CNY falling from 6.9931 to 6.648 on 2 Nov, a 4.9% drop for the dollar;
- USD/JPY at 159.93 on 13 Nov.
FXStreet (1 Oct) confirms the French-German 10-year spread at 130bp, the widest since 2012, and France's 2027 budget target of a 5%-of-GDP deficit. Wikipedia separately says it was confirmed in Oct 2026 that Lagarde would step down eight months early, in Feb 2027 (it gives no exact day). The ECB's press-release page could not be retrieved.

Reuters via Tribune (3 Aug): Japan and the US jointly bought yen on Friday 31 Jul. The yen had hit a 40-year low near 164 in July and rose more than 1% to 155.20. Bessent said the US will not hesitate to join further intervention. Tribune also reports Japan alone may have sold up to about $59bn the day before (Thursday 30 Jul). CFR (Brad Setser, 4 Aug): the US sold euro reserves to buy yen on 31 Jul, its first support for the yen since 1998. FRED H.10 data independently show:
- USD/JPY at 160.23 on 29 Apr, above 160;
- a 2026 high of 163.86 on 29 Jul;
- 159.47 on 30 Jul and 156.96 on 3 Aug;
- 159.93 on 13 Nov.
FXStreet (11 Nov): Japan sold a record ¥11.73tn of dollars in April-May; the Ministry of Finance page did not show amounts. FXStreet (25 Sep): the 10-year JGB yield briefly hit 3.11%, a 30-year high. FXStreet (16 Nov): USD/JPY about 159.50, and Q3 GDP shrank 0.1% annualised against an expected 0.3% gain; the Cabinet Office release could not be retrieved. The quote fix is in gca-11-quote.
